 ## Overview
-This method generates the base volumetric density field for cloud rendering by combining the structural continuity of Perlin noise with the billowy, cellular detail of Worley noise [S2]. It differs from standard procedural noise by storing multiple frequency levels of Worley noise in separate texture channels to allow for high-frequency detail reconstruction during runtime remapping, rather than baking all detail into a single low-precision channel [S2].
+This method generates the base volumetric density field for cloud rendering by combining the structural continuity of Perlin noise with the billowy, cellular detail of Worley noise [S4]. It differs from standard procedural noise by storing multiple frequency levels of Worley noise in separate texture channels to allow for high-frequency detail reconstruction during runtime remapping, rather than baking all detail into a single low-precision channel [S4].
 
